Judson obviously left out the mandatory "cu" or "poi" between "jetnu" and 
"zmadu"  He meant to say (I believe) "a sentence eviller than the preceeding", 
intending to mark his next utterance.  I think something along the lines of 
".ienai di'e zmadu di'u lo ka palci" was his intent.

  But now, on to my own take:

.i lo gerku [ku] fa'u lo mlatu cu jinvi le du'u lo remna cu pendo fa'u lante 
bo kargau

(note: the ku is not grammatically necessary, but jboski doesn't like it 
without it)
